  <h1>My Psychology Notes</h1>
    <h2>What Is Learning?</h2>
    <p>
•	Learning is the process of acquiring new knowledge, skills, attitudes, behaviours and experiences.
      <br>
•	It can happen through study, practice, observation or personal experience.
      <br>
•	Learning can lead to changes in knowledge, skills, behaviour and the way a person thinks.
      <h1>WAYS OF LEARNING </h1>
      <ol>Learning Through Formal
	 	Lesson</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning by attending formal lessons at school.</ul>
    <ul>•	Teachers provide knowledge, explanations and guidance.</ul>
    <ul>•	Classroom learning gives me a structured way of developing knowledge and skills.</ul>
    <ol>Learning Through Music</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning through listening to music.</ul>
    <ul>•	Music can expose me to different ideas, cultures and forms of expression.</ul>
    <ul>•	It can also help develop creativity and appreciation of different forms of art.</ul>
    
    <ol>Learning Through Historical
	 	Stories
</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning through historical stories.</ul>
    <ul>•	For example, stories such as Nambi and Kintu help me understand the past.</ul>
    <ul>•	Historical stories can teach lessons from the experiences of earlier generations.</ul>
    <ol>Learning Through Internet
	 	Research
</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning by conducting research on the Internet.</ul>
    <ul>•	The Internet gives me access to information beyond what is taught in class.</ul>
    <ul>•	Research helps me explore topics and improve my understanding.</ul>
    <ol>Learning Through Practice</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning through practice.</ul>
    <ul>•	Repeated practice helps me develop and improve skills.</ul>
    <ul>•	Practice also helps me apply what I have learned in real situations.</ul>
    <ol>Learning Through Movies and Educational Programmes</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning through watching movies and educational programmes</ul>
    <ul>•	They can provide information, examples and different perspectives.</ul>
    <ul>•	Visual materials can make some ideas easier to understand and remember.</ul>
    <ol>Learning From Other People's 	Experiences</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning from other people's experiences.</ul>
    <ul>•	I can learn by listening to their stories and observing what they have gone through.</ul>
    <ul>•	Their experiences can provide lessons that guide my own decisions.</ul>
    <ol>Learning From My Own
	 	Experiences
</ol>
    <ul>•	I have been learning from my own experiences.</ul>
    <ul>•	I reflect on what happens to me and consider what I can learn from it.</ul>
    <ul>•	My experiences can help me make better decisions in the future.</ul>
</p
  <h3>Conclusion</h3>
<ul>Learning does not only take place in a classroom.</ul>
<ul>•	It can happen through education, practice, observation, research, media and experience.</ul>
<ul>•	These different forms of learning help us gain knowledge, develop skills, change behaviour and improve our thinking.</ul>
